So, more questions, seems this thread took a detour;

Does the alcohol and water form a strong bond such that when heat drying the emulsion the water/alcohol leaves together or does the water and alcohol separate in the emulsion and evaporate individually upon heating.

I guess a better question is, if you leave a 90% alcohol bath open to dry air, will the alcohol evaporate and leave behind the water or does the alcohol and water evaporate together in those stable chains? How about the same experiment at different elevated temperatures?
